      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 📺 Source and Attribution\n\n**Duration represented:** approximately 20:56.\n\nLionel introduces a Candace Owens segment as the single best example of her explanatory ability and explicitly warns that he will stop it repeatedly to explain why particular moments matter. \n\nThe transcript does not contain speaker labels. Speaker changes are inferred from the setup, shifts in voice, direct reactions, and phrases such as “what I am about to show you” and “there you have it.”\n\nThis is therefore a strong structural reading, but individual sentence attribution should remain revisable when synchronized against the actual video.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
