      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧭 Central Observation\n\nThis is the first specimen that clearly exhibits a **media-reaction grammar**.\n\nLionel does not merely discuss Candace Owens. He selects a specific clip, starts it, interrupts it, identifies what he thinks the audience should notice, supplies comparisons and context, then resumes playback.\n\nThe reusable unit is not the whole episode. It is a repeated **commentary beat** connecting:\n\n1. a source-media range\n2. Lionel's reaction range\n3. the interpretive relationship between them\n4. a resume point back into the source\n\nThat strongly supports `Lionel Comments on Media` as a real node type.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
