        "markdown": "# 5 · Authenticity Interpretation\n## 8:57–13:52\n\nAfter the interview excerpt, the commentary focuses on whether Helen sounds credible, wounded, and sincerely dissatisfied with the investigation. Lionel argues that her emotional authenticity is self-evident and contrasts it with publicity, influencer campaigns, and what he characterizes as staged grief. \n\n**Function:** translate tone, demeanor, and emotional presentation into an interpretation for the audience.\n\n**Commentary role:** `interprets performance` plus `draws contrast`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
