          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 6 · Shared Grief Argument\n## 13:52–16:10\n\nThe source and Lionel's commentary converge on an explicit claim about expected grief: that rapid public appearances, tours, and cheerful institutional activity appear inconsistent with how most people would react after a spouse's violent death. \n\n**Function:** the reactor and source effectively co-author the conclusion.\n\nThis is not merely interruption. Lionel sometimes completes, intensifies, or ratifies the source's argument.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
