      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 8 · Audience Outro\n## 20:17–20:56\n\nLionel asks viewers to like, subscribe, verify that they remain subscribed, enable notifications, continue participating in the channel community, and comment with their own analysis. \n\n**Function:** convert the completed reaction into engagement and continued collective interpretation.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study03-stack",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Nested Media Stack",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -1040,
        "y": 450
      },
      "width": 590,
      "height": 470,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🪆 Nested Media Stack\n\nThis episode reveals that a media source cannot always be modeled as one flat video.\n\n## Level 1\n**Lionel episode**\n\nContains Lionel's setup, interruptions, commentary, synthesis, and outro.\n\n## Level 2\n**Candace Owens segment**\n\nThe primary media object Lionel is reviewing.\n\n## Level 3\n**NewsNation interview excerpt**\n\nA source embedded inside Candace's segment.\n\nA commentary node may therefore point to a source segment that itself references another source segment. Provenance and playback controls must survive this nesting.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study03-loop",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Commentary Beat",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -390,
        "y": 450
      },
      "width": 610,
      "height": 520,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🔁 The Reusable Commentary Beat\n\nThe smallest durable composition appears to be:\n\n1. **Play Source Segment**\n2. **Pause Source**\n3. **Lionel Comments on Media**\n4. **Classify the Commentary Role**\n5. **Resume Source**\n\nPossible commentary roles observed here:\n\n- identifies referent\n- supplies background\n- validates a comparison\n- adds analogy\n- interprets demeanor\n- intensifies a conclusion\n- defends the legitimacy of inquiry\n- evaluates the source's effectiveness\n\nA single node type could carry a `commentaryRole` property rather than requiring a different class for every rhetorical shade.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study03-types",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Provisional Node Types",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 280,
        "y": 450
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 540,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧪 Provisional Node Types\n\n## Strongest new candidate\n**Lionel Comments on Media**\n\nSuggested fields or relationships:\n\n- Lionel video source\n- Lionel commentary start and end\n- referenced source segment\n- source resume time\n- commentary role\n- speaker claim or interpretation\n- confidence or uncertainty\n- optional nested source reference\n\n## Supporting reusable types\n- **Lionel Frames Media**\n- **Lionel Summarizes Media**\n- **Media Source**\n- **Timed Media Segment**\n- **Transcript Segment**\n- **Embedded Source Segment**\n- **Playback Transition**\n\nThe episode template should compose these. It should not contain the transcript logic as one giant bespoke node.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study03-compare",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Comparison Across Three Studies",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 970,
        "y": 450
      },
      "width": 700,
      "height": 590,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🔬 Comparison Across Three Studies\n\n## Study 01 · Thesis Monologue\nLionel owns the complete structure and develops one central proposition through case study, context, synthesis, and prescription.\n\n## Study 02 · Hosted Forensic Commentary\nAnother host owns the container while Lionel performs a long anomaly audit, builds rapport, and answers a late direct question.\n\n## Study 03 · Annotated Media Reaction\nA specific external clip supplies the spine. Lionel alternates between playback and interpretation.\n\n## What now appears stable\n- frame an issue or source\n- identify what the audience should notice\n- add context and analogy\n- challenge an accepted narrative\n- recap or synthesize\n- invite continued audience inquiry\n\n## What varies\n- who owns the container\n- whether the spine is a thesis, evidence list, host prompt, or source clip\n- how transitions are generated\n- whether another speaker's media controls the pacing",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study03-implementation",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Implementation Implication",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1740,
        "y": 450
      },
      "width": 670,
      "height": 560,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🛠️ Implementation Implication\n\nThe earlier intuition now looks correct:\n\n**`Lionel Comments on Media` should probably be a node type with controls over a source-video node.**\n\nThe node should be able to:\n\n- play Lionel's commentary range\n- play the referenced source range\n- resume the source after the interruption\n- show both transcript ranges\n- reveal the commentary relationship\n- follow an embedded source recursively\n\nThe show template then supplies recurring segment nodes and composition rules. The shared layer supplies media playback, timestamps, transcript alignment, and provenance.\n\nThis is cleaner than forcing every show into one generic analysis template.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study03-confidence",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Current Confidence and Next Test",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": 1100
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 480,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-media-reaction-study-03"
        },
        "markdown": "# 📏 Current Confidence and Next Test\n\n## High confidence\n- this is a distinct media-reaction format\n- explicit pause-and-comment behavior is central\n- nested sources must be supported\n- a commentary node needs links to both reactor and source ranges\n\n## Medium confidence\n- one `Lionel Comments on Media` class with role properties is sufficient\n- framing and summarizing deserve separate node types\n\n## Still unknown\n- whether Lionel always comments in short beats or sometimes lets long clips run\n- whether he revisits the same source segment later\n- whether multiple source videos appear in one reaction episode\n- whether playback controls should live on the commentary node, source node, or a shared controller\n\nThe next media-reaction specimen should test those questions rather than merely confirming that pausing occurs.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786054301604,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    }
